Let me also check if there's a need to clear the filterShowAllView's text explicitly or if updateFilterView handles it. Looking at the code again:

```java
private void updateFilterView() {
    Context c = getContext();
    if (c == null) {
        return;
    }
    Set<GnssType> filter = PreferenceUtils.getGnssFilter();
    if (filter.isEmpty()) {
        filterGroup.setVisibility(View.GONE);
        // Set num sats view back to normal
        mNumSats.setTypeface(null, Typeface.NORMAL);
    } else {
        // Show filter text
        filterGroup.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
        filterTextView.setText(c.getString(R.string.filter_text, svVisibleCount, svCount));
        // Set num sats view to italics to match filter text
        mNumSats.setTypeface(mNumSats.getTypeface(), Typeface.ITALIC);
    }
}
```

When the filter becomes empty, the method hides the entire filter group and resets the satellite count styling, so I don't need to manually clear the text on the individual views. The build already confirms this compiles correctly, and the fix ensures the filter persists properly across restarts.
